      "name": "problem_severity",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.7,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Severity is a useful axis for explaining resolution-time variation. However, values are somewhat inferential: 'connectivity_blocking' vs 'partial_access' for terse descriptions like 'VPN connection issue' or 'Email system not working properly' involves guesswork not fully warranted by the text, though generally plausible."
    },
    {
      "name": "resolution_completion_status",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.3,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "This boolean is largely redundant with the existing 'state'/'closed_at' fields (a closed record is complete), so it adds little new analytical leverage for resolution-time comparison. Values are derivable from closed_at presence."
    },
    {
      "name": "incident_scope",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.7,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Scope (single user vs department vs system-wide) is a genuinely useful axis for explaining resolution time. Groundedness is mixed: 'WiFi in sales department' correctly maps to department-scoped, but 'Email system not working properly' -> 'system_wide_service' and 'VPN connection issue' -> 'single_user_affected' are inferences the terse text does not clearly support."
    },
    {
      "name": "authentication_access_failure",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.55,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A binary access-failure flag offers a modest additional cross-tab axis. Values in samples (all False for connectivity/email issues) are reasonable readings, though it is a fairly generic single-flag feature."
    },
    {
      "name": "technician_assignment_continuity",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.5,
      "source_groundedness": 0.4,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Assignment continuity could relate to resolution time, but the value is not derivable from the sampled source text (short_description/timestamps); it would require assigned_to vs closed_by comparison not shown. The True/False assignments in samples appear unsupported by provided evidence."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.68,
  "source_groundedness": 0.71,
  "rationale": "Several columns (infrastructure_domain, problem_severity, incident_scope) provide genuine new grouping axes well-aligned with the query about resolution-time variation, and are largely grounded in short_description. resolution_completion_status is largely redundant with existing state/closed fields. Groundedness is weakened by inferential severity/scope labels on terse text and by technician_assignment_continuity, whose values are not derivable from the sampled evidence."
